    {
      "name": "Trial by Jury",
      "type": "feature",
      "system": {
        "featureForm": "passive",
        "description": "<p>At the end of the proceedings, a jury votes whether to acquit or convict the party. When the court is called to order, have the prosecution present its case against the PCs and start a Countdown (9). It ticks down when a PC makes an action roll. When it triggers, the PCs and GM roll their Judgment Dice. If the party's total result meets or exceeds the GM's, the jury acquits them.</p><section id=\"secret-SR95wc6Tpalzj7Sw\" class=\"secret\"><p>Which PCs are put on trial? What are they accused of? What potential penalties would a guilty verdict bring?</p></section>",
        "attribution": {},
        "gmNotes": "",
        "resource": null,
        "actions": {
          "OuwNR2lTMCWW9xAm": {
            "type": "countdown",
            "name": "Start Countdown",
            "countdown": [
              {
                "name": "Trial by Jury",
                "type": "encounter",
