    {
      "name": "Counsel for the Defense",
      "type": "feature",
      "system": {
        "featureForm": "passive",
        "description": "<p>A PC can make an action roll to argue for their innocence (such as a Knowledge Roll to interpret the letter of the law, a Presence Roll to play on the jury's emotions, or an Instinct Roll to point out holes in the prosecution's case). On a success, the party gains a <strong>d6</strong> Judgment Die. On a critical success, they gain two. On a failure, the prosecution rebuts the PC's argument, and you gain a <strong>d6</strong> Judgment Die.</p><section id=\"secret-cESowB70gMt9UBRX\" class=\"secret\"><p>What is the weakest part of the prosecution's case? What is the strongest part of the party's defense?</p></section>",
        "attribution": {},
        "gmNotes": "",
        "resource": null,
        "actions": {},
        "granter": null
      },
      "_id": "5dfMCpOvnNNeUpNV",
      "img": "icons/magic/perception/hand-eye-fire-blue.webp",
      "effects": [],
      "folder": null,
      "sort": 0,
      "flags": {},
      "_stats": {
        "compendiumSource": null
      },
      "_key": "!actors.items!QbGEzb5Gvq36qYDj.5dfMCpOvnNNeUpNV"
    },
    {
      "name": "Counsel for the Prosecution",
      "type": "feature",
      "system": {
        "featureForm": "action",
        "description": "<p>The prosecution introduces a damning piece of evidence (such as an eyewitness testimony, test results, or a physical exhibit taken from the scene of the crime), and you gain a <strong>d6</strong> Judgment Die. A PC can mark a Stress to attempt a rebuttal of the evidence with a Knowledge, Instinct, or Presence Reaction Roll. On a success, the party gains the Judgment Die instead of you. On a failure, you gain an additional <strong>d6</strong> Judgment Die.</p><section id=\"secret-PKxc7LWA63hG6Dj0\" class=\"secret\"><p>Who leads the prosecution, and what is their relationship to the Time Council? What magic or technology does this court rely on to present and record evidence?</p></section>",
        "attribution": {},
        "gmNotes": "",
        "resource": null,
        "actions": {},
        "granter": null
      },
      "_id": "X91s1yNbX9BFGthV",
      "img": "icons/magic/perception/hand-eye-pink.webp",
      "effects": [],
      "folder": null,
      "sort": 0,
      "flags": {},
      "_stats": {
